From de94fbc6ba5ba44dee44c6ea6cf974a938f07f6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retrorepair <joelwhybrow@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:28:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 02/27] input: CRT lightgun tracker, calibration safety

GunCon 2 reports X = 0 (or 1 from stray light) while it sees no light.
Replace the flat 50 ms hold of the last position with a tracker that
decides from physical facts (lightgun_crt.cpp, unit tested on the host):

- loss of light in the interior of the picture is a dark frame: hold
  the last position (up to LIGHTGUN_CRT_DARK_MS)
- loss of light at an edge is the gun leaving the screen: offscreen now
- a trigger pull made while tracking opens a window
  (LIGHTGUN_CRT_SHOT_MS) in which dark reports are ignored and the
  valid report taken during the game's own flash is used
- a pull with no light stays offscreen (reload shots)

LIGHTGUN_CRT_TRACKER=0 in MiSTer.ini restores the previous behaviour.

Calibration:
- the GunCon 2 trigger (BTN_X) confirms an edge; the menu asked for it
  but only accepted A/B
- samples taken while the gun sees no light no longer reach the menu
- opposite edges closer than 16 raw units are rejected instead of saved
- a zero-width saved calibration falls back to the device defaults, and
  the scaling code no longer divides by zero on a min == max range

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit ee1ccc3902f18aa143c853fc5221055aad585895)
